# AmbientWeatherTemperatureViewer — AI Session Context

Copy this file to `CLAUDE.md` and fill in your personal details.
`CLAUDE.md` is gitignored so your infrastructure specifics stay private.

## What This Project Is

Personal weather monitoring web app. Pulls temperature from Ambient Weather cloud API, stores in
SQLite, visualizes with Chart.js. Single user, runs on a small cloud VM (e.g. GCP e2-micro free
tier) behind Tailscale.

- **Current page**: live sensor readings, auto-refreshes via `/api/current`
- **History page**: time-series chart (24h / 7d / 30d / 90d)
- **Compare page**: day-over-day overlay chart — HVAC effectiveness analysis
- **Patterns page**: snapshot at a specific time-of-day across months
- **Admin page**: channel config, collection status, manual backfill

## Stack

- Node.js 20 + Express 4 · EJS templates · Chart.js 4 via CDN · better-sqlite3 · node-cron
- Docker Compose · Tailscale host-install on VM

## Your Infrastructure

Fill these in after deploying:

- **GCP project**: `your-project-id`
- **VM name/zone**: `your-vm-name`, `us-central1-a`
- **Tailscale FQDN**: `your-hostname.your-tailnet.ts.net`
- **SSH**: `gcloud compute ssh your-vm-name --zone=us-central1-a --project=your-project-id --tunnel-through-iap`

## Critical Architecture Decisions (Do Not Revisit)

1. **Single container**: web server + collector in the same Node.js process.
2. **Synchronous DB**: `better-sqlite3` is synchronous — do not convert to async.
3. **Routes never call AW API**: all AW calls happen in `src/services/ambientWeather.js` on a schedule.
4. **Daikin is push-based (stub)**: `/api/ingest/daikin` returns 404 unless `INGEST_TOKEN` is set.

## File Map

```
server.js                       Entry point
src/app.js                      Express factory
src/collector.js                Cron: 5-min poll, weekly prune, startup backfill
src/db/schema.js                CREATE TABLE + default channel seed
src/db/index.js                 better-sqlite3 singleton
src/db/queries.js               All SQL query functions
src/services/ambientWeather.js  AW API client + rate limiting
src/services/mockData.js        Mock AW API (USE_MOCK_DATA=true)
src/routes/api.js               JSON API + Daikin ingest stub
src/routes/views.js             EJS page routes
views/                          EJS templates
public/style.css                All CSS
scripts/migrate-json-cache.js   One-time JSON cache migration
infrastructure/                 GCP setup + update scripts
```

## Ambient Weather API Constraints

- 1500ms minimum between calls · 288 records max per call (24h at 5-min intervals)
- Must chunk date ranges into 24-hour windows
- npm package: `ambient-weather-api@0.0.6`

## Local Development

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env   # no real keys needed for mock mode
USE_MOCK_DATA=true node server.js
# open http://localhost:3000
```

## Common Tasks

- **Manual backfill**: POST /api/admin/backfill `{"start":"YYYY-MM-DD","end":"YYYY-MM-DD"}`
- **Update on VM**: `cd ~/ambientweather && ./infrastructure/update.sh`
- **Backup DB**: `docker compose exec app sh -c 'cat /app/data/ambientweather.db' > backup.db`
